        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.735,
            0.647,
            0.756
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "12.3 Applications of Parallelograms"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.768,
            0.883,
            0.886
          ],
          "content": "We saw that parallelograms have several nice geometric properties. These properties make the parallelogram a versatile shape with many real-world applications. In physics, a fundamental law uses parallelograms to combine certain physical quantities like forces, as you will learn in a later year. Parallelograms are used in several mechanical linkages, such as the parallel motion linkage discovered by James Watt,"
        }
      ]
    }
